or","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and November to December came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those 75 years. In 2025 that pair landed at 36% of normal on the middle of the grids, while April to May ran 189%. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, with grid 18439 down at 47%. On grid 18738 the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 sits at 34.6, which is NOAA rain and not RMA&rsquo;s final index.</p>"}
